WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.624
At the end of the Tang dynasty, Zhu Wen gradually seized control of the army and the court's great power, becoming the most powerful man in the land.

00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:14.918
None of the court officials dared oppose his decisions.

00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:23.980
The young Emperor Ai sat on the dragon throne, but had completely lost his power and could only obey Zhu Wen's orders.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:32.466
In the year 907, Zhu Wen forced Emperor Ai to abdicate, ascended the throne himself as emperor, and founded the Later Liang.

00:00:32.816 --> 00:00:37.112
When the news spread, people everywhere were deeply shocked.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:42.814
The great Tang dynasty, which had lasted nearly three hundred years, formally perished from then on.

00:00:43.164 --> 00:00:50.868
But the Tang dynasty left behind countless beautiful poems and a brilliant, splendid culture.

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:57.170
The lights of Chang'an went out, but the radiance of Tang poetry forever shines upon later generations.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.600
A new era had begun, and history turned to a new page.

